The class implements the generated `OwnersApi` interface (OpenAPI). The route is `POST /api/owners`, mapped at class level with `@RequestMapping("/api")`. There is no separate POST-create in the v2 controller (`OwnerRestControllerV2.java` only exposes a paged list).

### 5. Duplicate check → 409 CONFLICT (same file, lines 215-220)

This is the existing 409 implementation. It's a private helper in the same controller, matching on **last name AND telephone**:

```java
private boolean isDuplicateOwner(Owner owner) {
    return this.clinicService.findOwnerByLastName(owner.getLastName()).stream()
        .anyMatch(existing ->
            Objects.equals(existing.getLastName(), owner.getLastName())
                && Objects.equals(existing.getTelephone(), owner.getTelephone()));
}
```

Note: it reuses `findOwnerByLastName`, whose repository queries use a `LIKE` prefix match (see item 3), so the exact `Objects.equals` on last name guards against prefix over-matching. It returns a bare `409 CONFLICT` with no body (no custom exception class is used — CONFLICT is produced directly via `ResponseEntity`). This is the **only** `HttpStatus.CONFLICT` usage in `src/main`.

